WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.600
When you think of Nazi Germany, you mostly
think about the human rights abuses, and the

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.160
concentration camps like Auschwitz.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.769
But have you ever wondered what happened to
the black people living under the Third Reich?

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:16.190
It turns out that even though there were racial
laws demanding the extermination of the Jewish

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:21.420
and Roma people, there were so few Africans
living in Germany, that they were not considered

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.340
to be one of Hitler’s main priorities.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.900
One very special mixed race boy grew up in
Germany during the Third Reich, and he lived

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:29.910
to tell the tale.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.210
Not only did he manage to survive unscathed,
but he also desperately wanted to join the

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.250
Nazi Party.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.310
He was an actual prince, and he grew up to
become a writer.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:45.000
This is the incredible story of Hans Massaquoi.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:57.440
Early Life
Hans-Jurgen Massaquoi was born in Hamburg,

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.110
Germany in 1926, but he didn’t look like
most of the blonde haired and blue eyed babies

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.480
born into the country.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.470
His mother, Bertha Baetz, was a German nurse,
and his father, Al-Haj Massaquoi was the prince

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:11.120
of the African country Liberia.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.720
When Hans was born, Al-Haj was a law student
studying at Trinity College in Dublin.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.300
The plan was for Bertha and Al-Haj to get
married after graduation, and she lived with

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.560
her future father-in-law, King Momolu.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.960
The King received his college education in
the United States, and he became the first

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.090
ethnically African diplomat to live and work
in Germany.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:33.040
Liberia had elected a president, so while
the position of King was still a powerful

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.409
one, he was more of a figurehead for the tribal
leadership.

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:39.710
For years, King Momolu had lived with five
wives, which was a tribal tradition.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:43.740
But he gave up that lifestyle in favor of
a more western way of life, and married a

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.330
woman named Rachel Johnson.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:50.000
They had several kids together, and they accepted
Bertha and Hans into their happy home.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.510
At that time, the only other mixed race children
living in Germany were called “The Rhineland

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.460
Bastards”.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.690
In 1919, Western Germany was occupied by the
Allies, which included Afro-French soldiers.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:04.420
The German women thought that these men were
exciting and exotic, and many of them had

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.180
affairs with the African soldiers.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:10.350
However, after the soldiers left Germany,
many of the women were pregnant, and they

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.520
gave birth to mixed race babies.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:17.190
People were shocked, and racist Germans were
disgusted that women would ever do this.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:20.980
Many of these mothers could not handle raising
the children alone, and they were called “whores”

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.910
for having these affairs.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:27.170
Children were given up for adoption, and the
government spread propaganda depicting black

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:28.510
men as rapists.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:32.099
These children were seen as a product of foreign
brutality.

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:36.090
However, only one woman out of the hundreds
of mothers to mixed race children ever came

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.640
forward to claim that she had been raped by
a black soldier, while the rest said that

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.310
they had a consensual romantic relationship.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:48.060
In the 1920’s, Germany's economy was struggling
to recover from World War I.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.970
The Massaquoi family were royalty, and they
were wealthy and exotic.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.880
This made them well respected in the city
of Hamburg, and they were treated by everyone

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.760
as esteemed guests.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.360
Bertha Baez got to experience living with
this royal treatment, and she was prepared

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.870
to move to Liberia to get married and have
a new life as an African princess.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:10.260
Unfortunately, Al-Haj abandoned Bertha and
Hans, and he never returned to Germany.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.990
King Momolu was furious with his son, and
he threatened to force Al-Haj to marry Bertha,

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:16.580
but she did not want that.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.780
Momolu agreed to continue to support Bertha
and his grandson in the consulate mansion

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.200
in Hamburg for as long as possible.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.200
When he was very young, Hans believed that
black people were the superior race.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.480
His family was wealthy, and most of the German
people were poor by comparison.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.080
They also had several maids and servants that
were all white.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.980
On top of that, Bertha’s friends would fuss
over him as a toddler and compliment his skin

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.220
wherever he went.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:44.640
Hans never met his father in person, and only
communicated with him through letters.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.000
So his grandfather stepped in to help raise
him, and he grew up having a very happy childhood.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.190
When he was seven years old, King Momolu was
asked by the President of Liberia to return

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:57.510
to his home country, and his duty as the German
consulate was over.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:01.340
He offered to bring Hans and Bertha to live
with him in Liberia, but she refused to leave

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.440
when she knew that Al-Haj did not want to
marry her.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:09.099
Bertha was an independent woman, and she decided
to go back to work as a nurse, and raise Hans

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:10.160
as a single mom.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:14.030
They moved to a working class neighborhood
in Barmbek, where they could only afford to

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:15.680
rent an attic apartment.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.970
Hans became friends with two boys in the neighborhood
named Fiete and Klaus, and they played together

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:20.970
every day.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:24.229
The three boys were good kids, and they got
to know many of the people in their town.

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:28.360
Even though he was able to make close friends,
Hans was bullied by the other boys in school

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.150
for the color of his skin.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:33.870
Children would taunt him with a racist rhyme
that is so offensive, we aren’t going to

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.139
repeat it in this video.

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:39.830
The children said that his skin was dirty,
and they said horrible things about his mother.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:43.840
Despite all of this bullying, Hans was incredibly
bright, and he was one of the smartest kids

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:44.969
in his class.

00:04:44.969 --> 00:04:48.680
He wanted to be an engineer when he grew up,
and he drew sketches of bridges from a very

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.689
young age.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:53.629
His teacher encouraged him to pursue this
career, even though she secretly thought that

00:04:53.629 --> 00:04:56.749
it would not be possible in Nazi-occupied
Germany.

00:04:56.749 --> 00:05:01.669
When he was 7 years old, Hans asked his babysitter
to sew a swastika patch on his sweater, so

00:05:01.669 --> 00:05:03.150
that he could wear it to school.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:06.330
He wanted to prove to all of his bullies that
he was a German.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:10.999
Of course, he was a child, and he didn’t
fully understand what being a “Nazi” meant.

00:05:10.999 --> 00:05:14.550
A photographer at the school snapped a picture
of him wearing the swastika.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:18.119
When Hans’ mother saw him wearing this when
he got home, she quickly removed the symbol,

00:05:18.119 --> 00:05:20.960
telling him that their family did not believe
in the Nazi party.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.919
However, like a lot of other kids, Hans rebelled
against his mother, and continued to try to

00:05:24.919 --> 00:05:27.020
fit in with the rest of the children in school.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:32.020
In 1935, when Hans was 9 years old, the Nuremberg
Laws were passed in Germany, which made it

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:35.889
illegal for Aryans and Non-Aryans to have
sex or get married.

00:05:35.889 --> 00:05:40.830
This included anyone who was not born with
pure German blood, which included Jews, Roma,

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:42.219
and of course, black people.

00:05:42.219 --> 00:05:45.069
Hans Massaquoi was classified as a “Non
Aryan”.

00:05:45.069 --> 00:05:48.140
His mother was sheltering him from learning
about the Nuremberg Laws, and she wanted him

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.310
to have a normal childhood.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:53.900
He could not understand why so many people
were being mean to him, and he wanted to know

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:56.539
why he couldn’t just be like everyone else.

00:05:56.539 --> 00:05:59.699
People would point and stare at him in the
streets, and whisper about the color of his

00:05:59.699 --> 00:06:00.699
skin.

00:06:00.699 --> 00:06:06.729
Back in the 1930’s, the slang term everyone
used for black people in Germany was the “N-word”.

00:06:06.729 --> 00:06:09.580
White people were calling Hans the N-word
all day, every day.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:15.979
He desperately wanted to fit in, and was willing
to go along with what everyone else was doing.

00:06:15.979 --> 00:06:22.699
Hitler Youth Envy
When Hans was in school, he sat in the classroom

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:24.279
together with the other German children.

00:06:24.279 --> 00:06:27.930
He was taught about how Hitler was a hero
who saved the nation from poverty, and how

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.779
Germany was the greatest country in the world.

00:06:30.779 --> 00:06:34.509
The minds of these young children were being
brainwashed.

00:06:34.509 --> 00:06:38.800
None of these kids knew that the Nazis were
killing and torturing innocent people, and

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.479
they grew up to be loyal followers of Adolf
Hitler.

00:06:41.479 --> 00:06:45.669
When boys turned 10 years old, it became mandatory
for them to join the Hitler Youth.

00:06:45.669 --> 00:06:49.300
From Hans’ perspective, the members of the
Hitler Youth wore cool uniforms, and it seemed

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.999
like joining a club similar to the Boy Scouts.

00:06:51.999 --> 00:06:56.550
Hitler Youth got to take days off of school,
and they marched in parades while crowds cheered,

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.179
and firework were set off in their honor.

00:06:59.179 --> 00:07:02.930
Propaganda posters were everywhere, and it
made it seem like the Hitler Youth were able

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:06.419
to play games all day and receive special
treatment.

00:07:06.419 --> 00:07:10.750
There was even a novel titled Hitler Youth
Quex that came out in 1932, and the movie

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.779
version premiered in 1933.

00:07:12.779 --> 00:07:16.780
Comic books and Disney movies were banned
in Germany, so these kids looked up to these

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:21.210
Nazi characters of propaganda as their heros,
instead.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:26.069
In 1936, Hans turned 10 years old, and he
believed that it was finally time for him

00:07:26.069 --> 00:07:27.369
to join the Nazi party.

00:07:27.369 --> 00:07:30.929
All of the boys in Hans’ school stood in
the yard, and their principal called out their

00:07:30.929 --> 00:07:35.360
names one by one to announce their official
enlistment in the Hitler Youth.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:40.590
Hans stood and waited in anticipation for
his name to be called, but it never was.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:43.860
Out of 800 kids, he was the last one left
standing.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:48.209
For anyone who has felt the pain of being
picked last in gym class as a kid, imagine

00:07:48.209 --> 00:07:51.929
that humiliation times a thousand.

00:07:51.929 --> 00:07:55.289
Determined to be included, Hans went with
his best friends to a Hitler Youth office

00:07:55.289 --> 00:07:59.470
in Hamburg to try to sign up, but they did
not allow him to join either, because he was

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:00.470
a non-Aryan.

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:05.059
The Nazis even began to hang signs in his
local playground, saying that non-Aryan children

00:08:05.059 --> 00:08:07.020
were no longer allowed to play there.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.949
His friend’s parents appreciated how badly
Hans wanted to join the Nazi party, which

00:08:10.949 --> 00:08:15.659
kept him in good graces with most of the adults
in his life.

00:08:15.659 --> 00:08:19.789
The one and only thing that could help restore
some of Hans’ pride in his heritage that

00:08:19.789 --> 00:08:23.839
year was the fact that an African American
runner named Jesse Owens dominated the Berlin

00:08:23.839 --> 00:08:25.930
Olympics in 1936.

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:29.949
This cause a huge scandal for the Nazis, who
were trying to prove to the world that their

00:08:29.949 --> 00:08:31.709
Aryan race was the best at everything.

00:08:31.709 --> 00:08:32.709
Years later, as an adult, Hans Massaquoi met
Jesse Owens in person and thanked him "for

00:08:32.709 --> 00:08:33.709
allowing me to walk a little taller among
my peers that summer."

